WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Welcome to our Send Your First FBA Shipment Training.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:10.000
We'll help you get started with FBA and learn how to send your first FBA shipment.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Fulfillment by Amazon or FBA is a great way to grow your business and reach more customers.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
With FBA, Amazon stores your inventory, ships your orders, and handles returns and customer service.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Your FBA products also become eligible for free shipping and Amazon Prime 2-day delivery.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.000
To register for FBA, sign in to Seller Central.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Hover over the Settings icon and select Account Info.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.000
From here, locate Your Services and click Manage.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Under You can sign up for, select Fulfillment by Amazon and click Register.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Next, you'll want to enroll in the FBA New Selection Program.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:58.739
Benefits of the FBA New Selection Program include free monthly storage,

00:00:58.739 --> 00:01:05.000
removals, and return processing for all eligible new to FBA parent ASINs.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:13.182
Sellers new to FBA can also get up to $200 for sponsored ads and a $100 discount on Amazon partnered

00:01:13.182 --> 00:01:14.000
carrier shipping.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:20.000
To enroll and learn more, search for FBA New Selection in Seller Central.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Now it's time to convert your existing listings to FBA.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.000
To get started, open the main menu in Seller Central.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Hover over Inventory, then click FBA Inventory.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.000
Go to the top menu, hover over Shipments, and click Send to Amazon.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:42.000
Now you can access these listings on the Send to Amazon page.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.000
On the Send to Amazon page, follow the steps in the workflow.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.000
The Send to Amazon workflow is broken down into the following steps.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.667
Step 1.

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:56.000
Choose Inventory to Send.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Step 1B.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Pack Individual Units.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.500
Step 2.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.000
Confirm Shipping.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.600
Step 3.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.000
Print Box Labels.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.143
Step 4.

00:02:08.143 --> 00:02:11.000
Confirm Carrier and Pallet Information.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.200
And Step 5.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.000
Print Pallet Labels.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:21.529
For more information on this workflow, search for Create Shipments with Send to Amazon in Seller

00:02:21.529 --> 00:02:22.000
Central.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:29.037
After your shipment is on its way to the fulfillment center, you can track its progress on the shipping

00:02:29.037 --> 00:02:32.000
queue page by clicking Manage Shipments under Shipments.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.000
This concludes our Send Your First FBA shipment training.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:41.000
You now have the tools to grow your business and get started with FBA.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.000
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
